[COMMENTS]
STATION,Trapezoidal critical depth flume. GENERAL: Structure capacity 2.25 cumecs, channel capacity is considerably greater but bypassing on left bank. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11). STATION HYDROMETRY: Power law rating in three sections. Records indicate it is based on hydraulic theory for a trapezoidal flume. Site is difficult to gauge at high flows due to the flashy nature of the catchment. FLOW RECORD: WY1980/1981 rejected because it was likely to have occured during period of missing data.
CATCHMENT,A relatively narrow catchment trending SE from headwaters in the High Weald (source is in Bedgebury Forest). Rural land use, some woodland - developed on Wadhurst Clay (about half) and the overlying Tunbridge Wells Sands.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged within 30% of QMED in December 2019. Flows observed to be within bank.
Pooling Suitability,No comment
[END]
